  "caption": "Quinn saw athletes in colourful tape and taped everything, including one ear. The sore shoulder didn't notice.\n\nResearch suggests kinesiology tape may give a small, short-lived drop in pain, and fake taping often does about as well. Its real value may be helping you feel supported enough to move.\n\nThings that often help: use tape as a cue alongside an exercise program, choose firm strapping or a brace if you've rolled an ankle before, peel tape off gently in the shower, and use the confidence to build strength.\n\nPain that wakes you, new numbness or weakness, calf swelling, or a spreading rash should be checked promptly.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
